Local files (not upstream)
--------------------------
xcoin_config.h   The build configuration, selected with MLK_CONFIG_FILE:
                   MLK_CONFIG_PARAMETER_SET 768 (ML-KEM-768 only);
                   MLK_CONFIG_NAMESPACE_PREFIX xcoin_mlkem768;
                   MLK_CONFIG_INTERNAL_API_QUALIFIER static (one compilation unit);
                   MLK_CONFIG_CUSTOM_RANDOMBYTES: mlk_randombytes calls xcoin_mlkem_randombytes;
                   MLK_CONFIG_CUSTOM_ZEROIZE: mlk_zeroize calls xcoin_mlkem_zeroize.
                 Every other option keeps upstream's default: no native backends
                 (MLK_CONFIG_USE_NATIVE_BACKEND_ARITH/_FIPS202 unset), no pairwise consistency
                 test on key generation (MLK_CONFIG_KEYGEN_PCT unset), stack buffers (no custom
                 allocator, so MLK_ERR_OUT_OF_MEMORY cannot occur), and upstream's empty-asm
                 value barrier for constant-time selection (verify.h; on compilers without GNU
                 inline asm upstream falls back to its volatile opt-blocker by itself).
xcoin_hooks.h    Declares the two hooks. Both are defined in src/pqrandom.cpp (bitcoin_util):
                   xcoin_mlkem_randombytes serves any length from GetStrongRandBytes in draws of
                   at most 32 bytes, the same loop as PQCLEAN_randombytes (GetStrongRandBytes
                   asserts on more, random.cpp ProcRand). Randomized key generation asks for
                   d || z in one 64-byte request, so d and z are two separate 32-byte draws, as
                   XIP-4 ("Secrets") requires; m is one 32-byte draw. It returns 0 (the node's
                   RNG aborts rather than fail); mlkem-native checks the result and returns
                   MLK_ERR_RNG_FAIL on non-zero.
                   xcoin_mlkem_zeroize is memory_cleanse. mlkem-native calls it on every stack
                   buffer it frees and, on failure, on its outputs.
mlkem768.c       The one compilation unit: defines MLK_CONFIG_FILE and includes
                 mlkem/mlkem_native.c (upstream's single-compilation-unit file).
